  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & I=\\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\frac{96 x^2 \\cos ^2 x}{1+e^x} d x \\\\ & 2 I=2 \\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 96 x^2 \\cos ^2 x d x \\\\ & I=96 \\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} x^2 \\cos ^2 x d x \\\\ & =48 \\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} x^2(1+\\cos 2 x) d x \\\\ & =2 \\pi^2+48(0-0)-48 \\int_0^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} x \\sin 2 x d x \\\\ & =2 \\pi^2-12 \\pi+[0-0]=\\pi\\left(2 \\pi^2-12\\right) \\\\ & =\\pi\\left(\\alpha \\pi^2+\\beta\\right) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow(\\alpha+\\beta)^2=100\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
